    ],
    "designDecisionsAndRationale": [
      "Reservation is the atomic commit point and launch authorization is single-use and fenced, preventing duplicate or uncertain execution.",
      "The dispatcher orchestrates dependency and host resolution but reuses the existing workflow runner, keeping RielaCore independent of RielaWork.",
      "Guard batches are durable before decision-making and the policy director is total and ordered, producing stable replay-safe outcomes.",
      "Human, policy, and bounded agent decisions share the store-backed applier so causality, task-version checks, cancellation, and completion cannot diverge by entry point.",
      "Capability placement fails before reservation and authoring uses the same reachable-node requirements, preventing validation from becoming a stale launch authorization.",
      "Auto-improve removal occurs only after equivalent dispatcher behavior and deterministic replacement examples pass.",
      "Parallel waves use distinct owners; Package.swift, schema, coordinator/applier, CLI, examples, documentation, lockfiles, and indexes transfer ownership only after predecessor acceptance and are reconciled serially."
    ],
    "intentionalTradeoffs": [
      "P1 keeps existing loop, routine, specialist, event dispatch, and their stores until later phases while replacing workflow-run auto-improve only after parity evidence exists.",
      "Enabled but unprobed capabilities remain usable as unverified, while pins never fall back and stale observations cannot authorize dispatch.",
      "Shared-workspace execution is retained; hash/change evidence and serial repair mitigate drift instead of introducing P4 worktree isolation."
    ],
    "supportedEdgeCases": [
      "Independent reservation races, insertion rollback, duplicate identities, stale task versions, uncertain launch authorization, and one-time pending rerun/recover consumption.",
      "Identical and conflicting decision replay, foreign or stale causal evidence, live cancellation acknowledgment, and last-admitted-attempt completion.",
      "Simultaneous guard violations, exact budget boundaries, replay deduplication, unreachable nodes, called workflows, pins, worker groups, capacity waits, stale probes, failed-auth explicit enablement, and corrupt profiles.",
      "Dry-run database byte/row equivalence, absent stores, deterministic examples, interrupt cancellation, and invalid or budget-blocked agent-director output."
    ],
    "outOfScopeEdgeCases": [
      "Compatibility migration for unrelated runtime databases or opening/resetting other sessions' stores.",
      "Recursive director repair, workflow-change proposals, replanning machinery, specialist chat classification, and long-lived supervision.",
